title: Flatbread
author: MaryJane Robbins
method: stovetop
source: https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/skillet-flatbreads-recipe
protein: none
servings: 10 to 12 flatbreads, depending on size
cook time: 30 minutes
prep time: 20 minutes
time required: 1 hour 0 minutes
alternative_name: Skillet Flatbreads
ingredient_count: 5
---

  Place the @King Arthur Unbleached All-Purpose Flour{3%cups (360g)}, @baking powder{2%teaspoons}, and @table salt{1 1/2%teaspoons} in a #large mixing bowl{} and stir to combine.

Add the @olive oil or vegetable oil{3%tablespoons (35g)} and @ice water{1%cup (227g)}, and mix to make a soft, cohesive dough. Adjust with flour or water as needed. The dough should be moist but not sticky. Cover with #plastic wrap{}, and let rest for ~{10%minutes}.

Preheat a #heavy-bottomed skillet{} on the stovetop. Add 1 tablespoon @vegetable oil{2 - 3%tablespoons (25g to 35g)} and heat until the oil starts to shimmer in the pan.

Divide the dough into 10 to 12 equal pieces. Each piece should weigh about 1 1/2 - 2 ounces, about the size of a large egg. Dredge each piece in flour, and roll to a rough circle or oval, about 1/4" thick. OR hand shape the pieces by flattening between your palms.

In batches, fry the flatbreads in the hot oil for ~{2-3%minutes}, or until golden brown. Flip and fry on the second side for another ~{2%minutes}. Transfer from the pan to a #rack{} to cool slightly before serving. Add more oil as needed for frying successive batches.